Concat is a free, open source video editor and a CapCut alternative.  It
covers what people open CapCut for: auto-captions, text to speech,
background removal, keyframe animation, effects and titles, multi-track
cutting and 4K export, with no watermark, no account and no upload.

Everything runs locally on a native Rust engine with a GPU compositor.
The AI models for captions (whisper.cpp), voices (Kokoro, Pocket TTS and
Chatterbox through sherpa-onnx and ONNX Runtime) and cutouts download
once from Settings and work offline after that.

It decodes and exports through FFmpeg (H.264, HEVC, AV1, up to 4K 60 and
10-bit colour), and everything the window does to a project can also be
done through its JSON-RPC API, on a socket or with the concat-cli tool.
